  "goodToKnow": "Die Geometrie is geometry. Basic German shapes: das Dreieck (triangle), das Viereck or Quadrat (square), der Kreis (circle), der Würfel (cube), die Kugel (sphere). Carl Friedrich Gauss and Bernhard Riemann made major contributions to non-Euclidean geometry, which later underpinned Einstein's theory of relativity. Geometrisch means geometric. Stressed on the last syllable. It has no plural."
